## 4. Mandatory Foundation Compliance Rules

<div class="portal-alert-box">
  <div class="portal-alert-title">CRITICAL FOUNDATION VIOLATIONS</div>
  <p>Pull Requests containing any of the following anti-patterns will be automatically blocked by Danger CI:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Direct SharedPreferences or AsyncStorage Usage:</strong> Never store authentication tokens, session secrets, or PII in unencrypted storage. Always use hardware KeyStore / Keychain via Foundation services.</li>
    <li><strong>Hardcoded Raw Color Hexes:</strong> Hardcoding hex colors like <code>#008544</code> inside UI views is strictly prohibited. All colors must reference theme palettes.</li>
    <li><strong>Uncontrolled Network Requests:</strong> Bypassing the network layer with raw <code>fetch()</code> or unpinned clients is blocked. All calls must traverse the TLS-pinned pipeline.</li>
    <li><strong>Silent Exception Swallowing:</strong> Empty <code>catch &#123;&#125;</code> blocks during bootstrap are prohibited. Unhandled startup failures must halt execution gracefully and display a diagnostic error viewport.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

